{
 "version": 1,
 "rule": "sync/pull-rounds",
 "_doc": "Scenarios run by server/internal/sync (B2) against one fresh database each. setup: workspaces (ref, user, language), entries (ref, language; created live), rows (ref, user, collection, workspace ref or null for user-global, entry/book ref, updatedAt (workspaces default to defaults.workspaceUpdatedAt; rows (keyed rows) use key = ref), deletedAt when the row is a tombstone — for books/bookmarks/highlights a library_deletions row instead of the row; dataString n makes a keyed row's data a JSON string of n 'x' characters; events carry type). The test writes rows with exactly these stamps. requests run in order with the server clock at now; query: collections (list, comma-joined), limit, workspace (a workspace ref or a literal id), since ($cursor = the cursor of the last completed round of this case), page ($next = the next token of the previous answer), tombstones (the literal value, \"1\" asks a round from no since for tombstones too); v=2 is implied. before: writes applied just before the request (op write: restamp a row's data at at; op delete: tombstone or delete-and-log at at; op insert: a new setup row). expect: status; error (the JSON error code); rows: per collection the row refs in page order (collections not listed are []); tombstones: refs that must come with deletedAt set; scope: whether scope is set (default: set on a request without page); scopeLanguages, scopeWorkspaces (refs, sorted by id); restarted (default []); catalogueChanged: scope.catalogue differs from the previous round's; keys: exactly these collection keys; more; cursorAt: the time inside the returned cursor (until - 30 s, only on the last page). more is false exactly when no row of the round remains (the server looks one row ahead), so only a round without rows ends on an empty page.",
 "defaults": {
  "workspaceUpdatedAt": "2026-11-12T07:00:00Z"
 },
 "budget": {
  "rows": {
   "min": 1,
   "max": 2000,
   "default": 500
  },
  "bytes": 4194304,
  "lagSeconds": 30
 },
